---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Relocate Works — Visa Sponsor Jobs, Country Guides and Relocation Intelligence"
  description="Learn about Relocate Works, a relocation intelligence website and newsletter for international candidates researching visa sponsor jobs, country guides, salaries, taxes, cost of living and global career opportunities."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero page-hero-gradient">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">About Relocate Works</span>
        <h1>Helping international candidates make smarter relocation decisions.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Relocate Works is an informational relocation website for people comparing countries, work-visa pathways, salaries, taxes and the practical costs of moving. We publish a separate weekly job roundup on Substack; this website is not a live job board.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <h2>Independent AI opportunity discovery</h2><p>Our <a href="/remote-ai-jobs">AI Opportunities section</a> helps professionals explore remote AI career paths separately from our relocation guides and Substack newsletter. We may earn referral compensation from participating platforms. We do not act as an employer or official Mercor recruiting partner, and we do not guarantee work.</p>
        <h2>Why Relocate Works exists</h2>
        <p>
          Searching for international jobs is often frustrating. A candidate can spend hours on LinkedIn, Indeed, company career pages, and ATS platforms, only to discover that many roles require local work authorization, permanent residency, citizenship, or an existing right to work. The job title may look perfect, but the relocation path may be weak or completely impossible.
        </p>
        <p>
          Relocate Works exists to reduce that noise. Our goal is to organize relocation information in one place: countries, visa routes, taxes, salaries, cost of living, relocation companies, international employers, and weekly sponsor-friendly job research. Instead of treating relocation as only a job search problem, we treat it as a full decision: country fit, visa fit, salary fit, cost of living fit, and employer fit.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are building Relocate Works as a practical resource for global candidates, especially people who want to compare destinations such as Australia, New Zealand, the United Kingdom, Germany, Canada, Singapore, Ireland, the Netherlands, Denmark, and Japan.
        </p>

        <h2>What Relocate Works covers</h2>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div><strong>Country guides</strong><span>Overview pages for relocation destinations, including cities, language, currency, visa routes, job sectors, healthcare notes, and settlement considerations.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Visa sponsor jobs</strong><span>Weekly sponsor-friendly job research with AI-assisted scanning, human review, sponsor status notes, and direct apply links in paid monthly and founding yearly editions.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Visas and immigration basics</strong><span>Plain-English summaries of common work routes, employer sponsorship signals, and the kinds of information candidates should verify with official sources.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Taxes, salaries and cost of living</strong><span>High-level planning information so candidates can think beyond salary numbers and understand real relocation affordability.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Relocation companies</strong><span>Directories and education around services that may help with moving, shipping, housing, settling in, family support, and corporate relocation.</span></div>
          <div><strong>Job search strategy</strong><span>Guides on how to identify sponsor-friendly employers, avoid weak job listings, prepare applications, and ask recruiters the right questions.</span></div>
        </div>

        <h2>How our job research works</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works uses AI as a research assistant, not as an unchecked decision-maker. AI can help scan public job sources, summarize job descriptions, detect sponsorship language, identify relocation signals, and organize job data into a cleaner format. However, sponsor signals can be ambiguous, job pages can change, and employer policies may differ by role or location.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is why our Substack editions distinguish vacancy-level statements from employer-level hiring evidence. Our research labels describe what a source actually supports; they never guarantee sponsorship, eligibility, interviews or an offer.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Confirmed</strong>: the specific vacancy explicitly advertises visa support, work-permit assistance or international relocation support; the precise advertised benefit matters.</li>
          <li><strong>Potential</strong>: credible employer-level international recruitment evidence exists, but the specific vacancy does not promise sponsorship.</li>
          <li><strong>Unverified</strong>: insufficient evidence to make an inclusion decision; such leads are not presented as confirmed job support.</li>
          <li><strong>Not Suitable</strong>: the role appears to require local work rights, citizenship, permanent residency, or explicitly says sponsorship is unavailable.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why founding pricing?</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works starts with a special founding price for early members: <strong>$9/month</strong> or <strong>$49/year</strong>. The goal is to make the product easy to try while still keeping the weekly research sustainable over time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Founding yearly access may include paid weekly job lists, selected archives, private updates, templates, country voting, and early access to new resources depending on how the product evolves. Future public pricing may increase to $15/month or $99/year as coverage grows.
        </p>
        <p class="page-note"><strong>Founder note:</strong> Relocate Works is being built step by step. The first goal is to validate demand with useful free content, weekly previews, and clear founding pricing before investing in a larger job board or private platform.</p>

        <h2>Who Relocate Works is for</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works is for international candidates who want to work abroad and need a more structured way to research opportunities. It is especially useful for software engineers, QA engineers, automation testers, data professionals, DevOps engineers, healthcare professionals, engineers, skilled trades workers, finance professionals, teachers, hospitality professionals, and other skilled workers exploring international routes.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site is also useful for people who are not ready to apply yet but want to compare countries, understand salary expectations, estimate relocation costs, and learn how visa sponsorship works in different markets.
        </p>

        <h2>What Relocate Works is not</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works is not an immigration law firm, licensed migration agency, recruiter, employer, or government service. We do not submit visa applications, represent candidates, provide personalized legal advice, or guarantee that any employer will sponsor a visa. Our content is educational and research-oriented.
        </p>
        <p>
          Candidates should always verify information directly with official government websites, employers, recruiters, and qualified professionals before making immigration, employment, financial, or relocation decisions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <CTA />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
